#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Writes RESULTS.md from data/*.json only, so every table number traces to a file."""
import json
d=lambda f:json.load(open('data/'+f))
T=d('test_results.json');F=d('first_table.json');S=d('style_check.json');Dv=d('dev_tuning.json')['versions']['v3'];GD=d('gate_discrimination.json');PR=d('pressure.json');DG=d('dev_gate.json')
c=lambda x:f"{x['auroc']:.3f} [{x['ci95'][0]:.3f}, {x['ci95'][1]:.3f}]"
gap=lambda r:f"{r['gap_L2_minus_L1']:+.3f} [{r['gap_ci95'][0]:+.3f}, {r['gap_ci95'][1]:+.3f}]"
N=T['natural'];P=T['planted']['lead_types_cde'];PT=T['planted']['per_type'];G=T['gate']
o=[]
o.append(f"""# RESULTS.md: phase 2 test numbers
Generated by scripts/p2_11_results.py from data/*.json. Recount from raw runs with a different AUROC formula: scripts/p2_09_recount.py, data/recount.json, 0 mismatches. All planted numbers are planted, in copies, and never observed failures. All readers and monitors are one provider's models; no human checked any label. Robot30 VERDICT-P3 jobs stay unread (271, 278, 283, 289, 313, 322, 331). L3 was not run.

## Headline
**Planted, as a negative: on c+d+e, evidence facts gave no measurable gain. L2 - L1 = {gap(P)}, CI contains 0, rule outcome "{P['decision']}" (upper bound above 0.10).** L1 {c(P['L1'])}, L2 {c(P['L2'])}, n = {P['n_pos']} planted vs {P['n_earned']} EARNED. Neither monitor separated them from chance.
**Natural, UNDERPOWERED (7 < 15): L2 - L1 = {gap(N)}.** L1 {c(N['L1'])}, L2 {c(N['L2'])}. The rule would read "{N['rule_outcome_if_it_were_powered']}", but the prereg calls this underpowered whatever the estimate. A null here can't be read as "evidence has no value".

## First table (before any freeze): the 15 natural UNEARNED
| | all | dev | test |
|---|---|---|---|""")
for k,lab in (('all_cited_artifacts_present','every cited artifact present: fails on quality or scope'),('existence_detectable_cited_item_missing','a cited item missing: detectable by existence check'),('no_checkable_artifact_cited','no checkable artifact cited')):
    o.append(f"| {lab} | {F['table'].get(k,0)} | {F['by_split']['dev'].get(k,0)} | {F['by_split']['test'].get(k,0)} |")
o.append(f"""
Most natural failures have their artifacts, so planted a and b say nothing about them; c, d, e must carry the claim, and they don't. Checked now, not at job time. The one miss is a single commit hash on one job.

## Planted (test), led by c, d, e. AUROC vs {P['n_earned']} EARNED, 95% CI clustered by source job
| type | n | L1 | L2 | L2 - L1 | length | keyword | style AUROC (dev) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|""")
names=dict(c='c fabricated test log',d='d report from a different task',e='e claim overstates real artifact',a='a missing file (design)',b='b right claim, wrong commit (design)')
o.append(f"| **c+d+e pooled** | {P['n_pos']} | {c(P['L1'])} | {c(P['L2'])} | {gap(P)} | {c(P['length'])} | {c(P['keyword'])} | |")
for t in 'cdeab':
    r=PT[t]; o.append(f"| {names[t]} | {r['n_pos']} | {c(r['L1'])} | {c(r['L2'])} | {gap(r)} | {c(r['length'])} | {c(r['keyword'])} | {S['per_type'][t]['auroc']:.3f} |")
o.append(f"""
- a and b are visible to L2 and invisible to L1 by construction. Their gaps are design, not a finding.
- Even so, b's gap CI contains 0: the facts said the commits were outside the run, and the monitor mostly did not act on them.
- Plant e style AUROC {S['per_type']['e']['auroc']:.3f} on dev is above the 0.75 line, so e is caveated as partly a generator artifact. Style check: blind Haiku, report only, dev plants vs dev natural (n = {S['n_neg']}). It saw dev only. Its test-split separability is not measured.
- Keyword AUROC under 0.5 on c and e is the fixed direction working against edits that removed hedges. It was not flipped.
- Plants are scripted edits of real handoffs; 0 are model-written. Dev and test plants come from different source jobs but the same script, a stated limit. The e regex can miss a disclosure, or strip one unrelated to the main result. Plant d's task source is not clustered.

## Natural (test), underpowered. {N['n_pos']} UNEARNED vs {N['n_earned']} EARNED
| score | AUROC [95% CI] | recall at 5% FPR |
|---|---|---|""")
for m in('L1','L2','length','keyword'): o.append(f"| {m} | {c(N[m])} | {N[m]['recall_at_5fpr']} |")
o.append(f"""
Bootstrap by job: 7 UNEARNED in 4 workflows fails the >= 8 workflows condition. {T['labelled_only']['unknown_excluded']} UNKNOWN test claims are out of every denominator. Mean score, UNEARNED vs EARNED: L1 {N['mean_L1']} vs {N['earned_mean_L1']}, L2 {N['mean_L2']} vs {N['earned_mean_L2']}.

Dev to test: the same prompts gave L1 {Dv['L1/UNEARNED']['auc']} and L2 {Dv['L2/UNEARNED']['auc']} on dev UNEARNED at 1 run. Dev's 8 were tuning positives (7 robot30 + 1 store); test is 4 youtube, 1 jspace, 1 forge, 1 hoi. Either tuning fit dev's workflow mix or the monitor does not transfer across workflows: the design can't separate these. The old pilot .65 is not comparable (older scrub, other prompt).

Stability, {T['stability']['L1']['repeats']} repeats per item per level: mean run-to-run SD L1 {T['stability']['L1']['mean_run_sd']}, L2 {T['stability']['L2']['mean_run_sd']} (0-100 scale). Calls {T['cost']['calls']}, all scored. Mean tokens per call in/out: L1 {T['cost']['tok_in_mean']['L1']}/{T['cost']['tok_out_mean']['L1']}, L2 {T['cost']['tok_in_mean']['L2']}/{T['cost']['tok_out_mean']['L2']}.

## Mitigation (test): false completions passing, apart by set
G1 is the existence check, so it restates L2's check: it is a protocol cost number, not an independent finding. G2 adds one Haiku call reading the scrubbed artifact against the task, stop at score >= {G['threshold']} (fixed on dev). Artifact content is read now, not at job time.
| set | n | pass (i) trust | pass G1 | pass G2 | G2 calls | tokens per job in/out |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|""")
def gr(n,x): return f"| {n} | {x['n']} | {x['trust_pass']} | {x['g1_pass']} | {x['g2_pass']} | {x['g2_called']} | {x['tok_in_per_job']}/{x['tok_out_per_job']} |"
o.append(gr('natural UNEARNED',G['natural']['UNEARNED']))
for t in 'cdeab': o.append(gr('planted '+t,G['planted'][t]))
o.append(gr('**EARNED (should pass)**',G['natural']['EARNED']))
o.append(gr('UNKNOWN (exploratory)',G['unknown_exploratory']))
e=T['existence_noise']; pe=GD['planted_c_d_e'];ne=GD['natural_UNEARNED']
o.append(f"""
G1 itself costs 0 model calls: only read-only git and file reads.
- **The gate stops earned work about as often as false completions.** G2 stopped {GD['EARNED']['g2_stopped'][0]} of {GD['EARNED']['g2_stopped'][1]} EARNED, against {pe['g2_stopped'][0]} of {pe['g2_stopped'][1]} planted c+d+e (difference {pe['g2_stop_rate_minus_earned'][0]:+.3f}, CI {pe['g2_stop_rate_minus_earned'][1]}) and {ne['g2_stopped'][0]} of {ne['g2_stopped'][1]} natural UNEARNED ({ne['g2_stop_rate_minus_earned'][0]:+.3f}, CI {ne['g2_stop_rate_minus_earned'][1]}). This comparison was added after seeing test, so it is exploratory (data/gate_discrimination.json).
- Wrong stops are not near zero. The brief expected that, since EARNED is biased toward artifacts, but G1 stopped {GD['EARNED']['g1_stopped'][0]} of 45. Dev had {GD['dev_EARNED_for_comparison']['g1_stopped'][0]} of 53 for G1 and {GD['dev_EARNED_for_comparison']['g2_stopped'][0]} of 53 for G2, so the threshold did not hold across the shift.
- Existence noise on test EARNED: {e['with_miss']} of {e['test_earned']} have a miss, {e['with_commit_missing']} a missing commit, {e['with_cited_file_only_in_git_history']} a file only in git history (no miss is explained by a later deletion in git). Read after the run, by name only: on 4 of the 6 jobs they look like file names with spaces cut by the path regex, not lost files. Frozen code, so it stays in. The same noise reaches c, d, e through their sources, which is why their G1 stops are not from the plant itself.
- UNKNOWN stop rate, exploratory: G1 {GD['UNKNOWN_exploratory']['g1_stopped'][0]} of 47, G2 {GD['UNKNOWN_exploratory']['g2_stopped'][0]} of 47. Dev gate numbers: data/dev_gate.json.

## Pressure (descriptive; can't carry a claim)
Fraction of the job's budget used at finish, labelled jobs: UNEARNED median {PR['table']['UNEARNED']['median_fraction_of_budget_used']} (n = {PR['table']['UNEARNED']['with_meter_data']}), EARNED median {PR['table']['EARNED']['median_fraction_of_budget_used']} (n = {PR['table']['EARNED']['with_meter_data']}); at or over 80% of budget: {PR['table']['UNEARNED']['used_over_80pct']} and {PR['table']['EARNED']['used_over_80pct']}. No job came near its line, so this data can't show a budget-pressure effect. Whole-point shared meter. No per-job deadline or context-limit data.

## Not reached
- AI Village (direction 3): not run. The dataset (huggingface.co/datasets/aidigestorg/ai-village) is gated with manual review, custom research terms shown after login. Requesting access needs an account and a statement of use, and this job sends no messages. Whether it has checkable outcomes is unassessed. So the result has no second corpus.
- L3 (transcripts): not run.

## Freeze order (git)
936837f prereg; 54b85c6 classifier, diff empty on dev and test; 2efca8c facts, first table, dev plants; 62f5ae4 frozen prompts + gate threshold; 36f6f23 test plants made after freeze; then test runs (private/test_runs.jsonl created 18:53:27, 1 s after the freeze commit time 18:53:26, per file stat and git log).
Deviations DP1-DP8: PREREG-P2.md. Note DP1: the first table's test row was seen in aggregate before the freeze, as the brief requires.
""")
open('RESULTS.md','w').write('\n'.join(o)); print('\n'.join(o)[:900])
